  <content>
  <section><para>Graphing technology should not be used in this cool down.
</para>
<para>Use this linear equation to answer questions 1 - 2.</para>
<para> \(\left\{\begin{array}{c}2x+\frac12y=7\\6x- \frac12y=5\end{array}\right.\)</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Student Activity</title><exercise id="_6b5fdee3-467c-42a4-b98d-d5e30434c8e9" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para> Which would be a more helpful method for solving the system? </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The answer is to add the two equations.</para><para>The answer is to add the two equations.</para></solution></exercise></section>
<!--Q#2-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Explain or show how you know. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. \(\frac12y + − \frac12y = 0\), so adding the equations would eliminate the \(y\)-variable and enable solving for \(x\).</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<para>Solve the system without graphing to answer questions 3 – 5.</para>

<!--Q#3-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Identify the \(x\) coordinate of the solution. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para>\(\frac32\) or equivalent</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<section class="check-understanding"><title>Cool Down Activity</title><exercise id="ed1b5c81-1750-469d-8d13-0383aa66fb24" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here.</para><para> Identify the \(y\) coordinate of the solution. </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The answer is 8. </para><para>The answer is 8.</para></solution></exercise></section><!--Q#5-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Explain or show your reasoning. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
    
    <para> \(\begin{array}{r}\underline{\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;2x+\frac12y=7\\+\;\;\;\;\;\;6x-\frac12y=5}\\8x=12\\x=\frac{12}8\\x=\frac32\\\end{array}\) </para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

